Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Alamut project.

## What was implemented:

1. **Installed @vercel/analytics package**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to project dependencies
   - Package installed via npm and package-lock.json updated

2. **Configured Analytics component**
   - Modified: `src/App.tsx`
   - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
   - Added `<Analytics />` component to the app's root ErrorBoundary
   - Component placed alongside other global UI components (ToastHost, ConfirmHost)

## Implementation details:

- **Framework**: Vite + React
- **Documentation source**: https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart (fetched 2025-05-15)
- **Installation method**: Following official Vite/React integration pattern from Vercel docs
- **Package manager**: npm (based on existing package-lock.json)

The Analytics component was added to App.tsx after the ToastHost and ConfirmHost components, ensuring it tracks all routes and user interactions across the application.

## Testing performed:

✅ TypeScript typecheck passed (npm run typecheck)
✅ Production build successful (npm run build)
✅ All 438 unit tests passed (npm test)
✅ No breaking changes introduced

## Next steps:

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard (Analytics section)
2. Deploy the application using `vercel deploy`
3. Verify analytics tracking by checking browser Network tab for `/_vercel/insights/view` requests
4. Monitor analytics data in the Vercel dashboard

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation and preserves all existing code structure and functionality.
